 "notes": [
  "A first-quarter filing has no balance sheet: the model starts from the audited 31 March 2026 balance sheet, read from the company's own copy of its year-end results.",
  "Volume is cement and clinker sold together (the company sells clinker too), so the realisation per tonne and the costs per tonne are on both; the utilisation that comes out is not the plants' own.",
  "Freight is the two carriage lines added: on finished goods and on clinker moved between its own plants.",
  "The model has no row for exceptional items: the past folds them into other expenses (a cost is added, a gain taken off), so the model's profit before tax is the filing's. FY26's exceptional charge (1,131.97, revised wages) is in other expenses.",
  "The filing does not split interest on leases out of finance costs, so all of it is interest on borrowings and the rate on borrowings that comes out is high; interest on leases is left at nil."
 ],
